      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I agree with you Samiscool51 i seem to be unable to add a avatar in VR despite my tries and i mean i tried!(i watched videos and followed each step to the T) but i cant grasp Unity im not as computer inclined as most are im use to console so everything is very confusing when it comes to these things i would just be happy if they made it more easier for those who CANT use Unity or for what ever reason are UNABLE to add in models through the multi step process where if you mess up you have to completely scrap it and start over... im just saying if VRchat was to grow they should make it more easier for those who cant do all the steps needed to add their OWN models (including if its a shared computer) and \ni know they could go in the worlds made for avatars but think about it, just to get for one model they have to find the world with the model, then they have to find the model its self then after that they can go out and have fun... IDK if its just me but that seems too much of an hassle for just ONE model!!! A model you prob wont use again. and for me it kinda puts me out of the mood to even play the game, and sorry if you dont agree with me but its just to much of a hassle including if you already dont have a lot of time to even stay on the game for long it kinda sucks :/\n\nEdit: or at least add a feature where you can save your current model and have a tab where you can pick it from if the Dev's for what ever reason cant make it easier to add your own models in",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
